\subsection{Suspension Policy and Availability}
\label{sec:suspension-policy}
With immediate suspension, one member's requests withdraw the disputed facts across ten sites and take exports from the approved ACEs to zero, while the services keep answering; under two-reporter suspension the first report is retained and the second opens the dispute, duplicate reports add no votes, and local vetoes recorded during withdrawal survive restoration with fresh commits required for export. [-\textbf{[PLACEHOLDER: withdrawal-time and read-throughput figures-]{+One identity's 100 disputes withdrew 1,000 site records in a median 5.2~s, cutting concurrent read throughput from 662+} to [-remeasure on the final service.]}-]{+228 operations/s.+}

\subsection{Candidate Selection on Captured Traffic}
\label{sec:utility-results}
@@ -549,19 +549,19 @@ The operating point chosen from the adversarial bound is not the one that maximi

Recovery requires approval validity and revocation origin, whether represented through states or history. The mutations (Table~\ref{tab:tla}) and the restoration-policy ablation (Sec.~\ref{sec:lifecycle-results}) expose failures when this information or its checks are omitted. The review process still requires evaluation with operators.

Candidate selection can adapt without changing local authorization or recovery. Quorum accounts for most queue reduction at US/UK; ordering explains the advantage over unranked pooling. Threshold-then-rank suits deployments that maintain the bounded raw-breadth share assumption of Criterion~\ref{crit:poison-bound}. Trust weighting and clustering mitigate tested identity inflation but fail under padding. Ranked union yields [-slightly more-]{+at least as many+} receiver-observed endpoints at matched [-budgets,-]{+budgets (35/39/40 vs.\ 35/37/37),+} but no tested policy establishes benignity or necessity. Review capacity should inform the retention window $W$, whose practical value remains open.

Local control does not eliminate withdrawal's availability costs. One reporter can interrupt service under immediate suspension; requiring two preserves permissions until corroboration but delays withdrawal if no second report arrives. Both policies remain vulnerable to collusion, and the prototype lacks dispute rate limits and reputation penalties. Unreachable gateways can retain stale rules until reconnection, with no[-established-] withdrawal deadline [-while unreachable (after reconnection, the median convergence stayed within its bound in every measured cell). In the prototype-]{+meanwhile. A site can record+} a {+veto offline, but its+} local [-revocation looks up the fact at-]{+restore reads+} the evidence service [-first, so a site that cannot reach it cannot record a veto until-]{+and is refused while+} it [-reconnects.-]{+is unreachable, unlike in the model.+}


The shared evidence service is a[-throughput bottleneck and-] single point of failure for candidate flow and withdrawal [-propagation.-]{+propagation, and every site's commit reads it twice.+} It holds no local authorization state: failure can delay withdrawal but cannot[-itself-] grant or revoke local [-permissions. Replication and recovery remain-]{+permissions; replication remains a+} deployment [-concerns. Co-located experiments-]{+concern. Experiments+} emulate delay and loss on[-one host pair rather than measure-] a [-real wide-area network,-]{+single host+} and [-do not evaluate-]{+use no+} production [-workloads;-]{+workload;+} finite models assume authenticated [-callers, and-]{+callers;+} gateway tests disable signature [-validation.-]{+validation, and withdrawal there stops only new connections.+} Deployment requires the authentication, roles, and signing integration in Sec.~\ref{subsec:trust}.

The pseudo-site partition and six-type alignment restrict generalization. Coverage of fleets using these mechanisms remains unverified.


\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:conclusion}
This paper presented DIB for managing locally authorized MUD policies from shared IoT observations. [-Finite-model-]{+Bounded model+} checks and[-guard-removal-] mutations assess its [-authorization lifecycle;-]{+lifecycle,+} OpenWrt/osMUD [-tests demonstrate enforcement. Outage-]{+episodes measure withdrawal at the gateway, and outage+} experiments show that one collapsed update preserves[-local-] vetoes and invalidates stale [-approvals after a missed withdrawal and restoration episode. Candidate-selection and suspension experiments quantify review volume and availability costs.-]{+approvals.+} Future work will evaluate operator review, mechanisms to bound gateway withdrawal time, and recovery of the shared evidence service.

